{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Partners appeals to me because vocal duets feel connected to the vocal holiday albums I chose before.",
    "That connection gives me a reason to try a nonholiday album while staying close to the singing I currently enjoy."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The rock compilations and heavier albums do not offer the vocal ensemble listening I want right now.",
    "Adele's albums and the other pop choices feature singing, but emotionally intense ballads or pop rock do not feel like the same experience as the vocal albums I have been choosing."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices seem to assume that interest in a few vocal albums means I want a broad range of pop and rock.",
    "Familiar names and hit collections seem to count for too much; recognition alone would not make me choose an album."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated Christmas album choices suggest that the seasonal listening occasion mattered, not just the presence of vocals.",
    "My latest choice, The New Old Fashioned, makes vocal ensemble music a more convincing next step for me than a general selection of well-known singers."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "Partners connects with my interest in vocal music, but most of the list stretches that interest too broadly into pop and rock."
}"}
